        "original_id": "e25974ba-bfbf-5bff-ba02-b109d4dacd03",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Friedrich Ratzel, Rudolf Kjellén\n- Concepts: Lebensraum\n- Organizations: Nazi Party, Nazi Germany\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Friedrich Ratzel was a German geographer and ethnographer who lived from August 30, 1844 to August 9, 1904.\n- Friedrich Ratzel was notable for first using the term Lebensraum in the sense that the National Socialists later adopted.\n- Rudolf Kjellén's work was influenced by Friedrich Ratzel.\n- The Nazi Party and Nazi Germany supported the most extreme form of the Lebensraum ideology until the end of World War II.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
