        "text": "Page: Friedrich Ratzel. Sentence: Friedrich Ratzel (August 30, 1844 – August 9, 1904) was a German geographer and ethnographer, notable for first using the term \"Lebensraum\" (\"living space\") in the sense that the National Socialists later would.\nPage: Lebensraum. Sentence: The most extreme form of this ideology was supported by the Nazi Party (NSDAP) and Nazi Germany until the end of World War II.\nPage: Rudolf Kjellén. Sentence: His work was influenced by Friedrich Ratzel.",
